  {
   "title": "Repair: one variable per precedence level",
   "explain": "Give each precedence level its own variable, nested so that the tighter operator sits deeper in the tree. The left recursion (E → E + T) makes each operator group to the left, so only one tree is left.",
   "lines": [
    "operators, loosest first: +   <   ×   (the usual precedence; swap the levels to swap it)",
    "level 1: E → E+T | T     (+ group to the left; anything tighter sits below, in T)",
    "level 2: T → T×F | F     (× group to the left; anything tighter sits below, in F)",
    "atoms: F → a",
    "P′: E → E+T | T",
    "P′: T → T×F | F",
    "P′: F → a",
    "same language: compared on every string of length ≤ 10 ✓",
    "one tree per string: checked for every string of length ≤ 8 ✓",
    "a+a×a now has ONE tree: E ⇒ E+T ⇒ T+T ⇒ F+T ⇒ a+T ⇒ a+T×F ⇒ a+F×F ⇒ a+a×F ⇒ a+a×a"
   ],
